---
// /brands/true-residential-outdoor-refrigerator-repair/ — Luxury Wave L-3. True Residential
// OUTDOOR refrigeration. NEW. Slots into the outdoor-refrigerator brand family (perlick/
// sub-zero/u-line/viking outdoor). True Residential = home line of True (independent
// American-made since 1945 — matches existing true.astro framing, verified correct;
// NOT Middleby). Outdoor UL-rated line: 24" glass-door outdoor fridges, outdoor fridge/
// freezer drawers, outdoor beverage centers, 15" outdoor ice makers, outdoor wine cabinets;
// commercial-grade 300-series stainless + forced-air. Residential/commercial disambiguation.
// $89 (outdoor). NO sourced failure. Verified: agent C (True Caliber heritage, BBQGuys, Wilshire).
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ServiceHero from '../../components/ServiceHero.astro';
import BrandBranchesGrid from '../../components/BrandBranchesGrid.astro';
import { MAIN_PHONE, MAIN_PHONE_TEL } from '../../data/branches';
import { mergeCredentials } from '../../data/credentials-schema';
import { BRANCH_LOCATIONS_GEO_NEUTRAL } from '../../lib/build-location-array';
import { OPENING_HOURS_SCHEMA } from '../../data/business-hours';

const title = "True Outdoor Refrigerator Repair Los Angeles";
const description = "True Residential outdoor refrigeration repair across Los Angeles — UL-rated refrigerators, drawers, beverage centers and wine cabinets. $89 diagnostic.";
const canonical = "https://samedayappliance.repair/brands/true-residential-outdoor-refrigerator-repair/";

const faqs = [
  { q: "Is this the same True as the commercial refrigerators in restaurants?", a: "Same company, different line — and it's worth being clear. True is an independent, American-made refrigeration manufacturer that's built commercial refrigeration since 1945; True Residential is its home line, which adapts that commercial-grade engineering for the house. This page is about True Residential's outdoor refrigeration — the UL-rated outdoor refrigerators, drawers, beverage centers, ice makers, and wine cabinets built for patios and BBQ islands. If you're a restaurant or bar with a True commercial unit (T-series, TUC, TSSU, GDM), that's our commercial True refrigeration service instead. For a home outdoor True, this is the right page, and it's residential scope: $89 diagnostic, waived with repair." },
  { q: "What makes a True outdoor unit different from an indoor one?", a: "Every True undercounter unit is engineered UL-rated for outdoor use, which is exactly what a patio or BBQ-island fridge needs — the outdoor models are built to handle the temperature swings, humidity, and heat load that would overwhelm an indoor-rated fridge left outside. True builds them commercial-grade: 300-series stainless steel and forced-air cooling that moves cold air aggressively enough to hold temperature even on a hot LA afternoon with the sun on the cabinet. That's the same forced-air, heavy-duty approach True uses in its commercial refrigeration, brought to the backyard. When one struggles, it's usually the forced-air cooling system, the condenser, or the controls — all diagnosable and repairable." },
  { q: "My True outdoor refrigerator isn't cooling on the patio — what's wrong?", a: "On a True outdoor unit that won't hold temperature, our techs work the same order as any refrigeration diagnosis, tuned for the outdoor environment: dirty condenser coils (outdoor units pull in more dust, pollen, and debris than indoor ones, so coils clog faster and cooling drops), the condenser or evaporator fan, the forced-air system, the defrost components, the controls, and on the serious end the sealed system or compressor. Heat load matters outdoors too — a unit in direct afternoon sun on a black BBQ island works harder, so we check that the installation gives it airflow. Cleaning coils and confirming ventilation are the first moves; the sealed system and controls are our techs' work. $89 diagnostic, waived with repair." },
  { q: "Which True outdoor products do you service?", a: "The full outdoor line — 24-inch glass-door and solid-door outdoor refrigerators, outdoor refrigerator and freezer drawers, outdoor beverage centers, 15-inch outdoor ice makers, and outdoor wine cabinets. These live in cabanas, pool houses, and BBQ islands across the Westside and the estate belt, and they're serviced on the same refrigeration principles — condenser and coils, forced-air cooling, fans, defrost, controls, sealed system — with the outdoor environment factored in. The ice makers add their own water-path and ice-harvest diagnosis. Tell us which unit and its symptom and we'll bring the likely parts." },
  { q: "Is a True outdoor unit worth repairing?", a: "Almost always. True Residential outdoor refrigeration is premium — columns and outdoor units run well into five figures, and side-by-side configurations higher — built commercial-grade to last. That combination makes repair-versus-replace an easy call: a coil cleaning, a fan, a control, or a defrost part is a fraction of replacement, and the unit is engineered for a long service life. True is also an active American manufacturer with real parts support and a strong LA service footprint, so there's no orphan-brand parts problem. We'll give you the honest number, but on a True outdoor unit the answer is nearly always repair." },
  { q: "Do you cover True outdoor units across the Westside and beyond?", a: "Yes — same-day in most cases across Los Angeles, Beverly Hills, Malibu, Newport Beach, and the wider Westside and coast, with our branches covering Orange County, Ventura, San Bernardino, and Riverside. True outdoor refrigeration clusters where the outdoor kitchens are — the estate belt, the beach cities, and pool-house properties — which are well within our densest service areas. We answer the phone 24/7 and carry the common refrigeration parts. $89 diagnostic, waived with repair." }
];

const schema = { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@graph": [
  { "@type": "Service", "serviceType": "True Residential Outdoor Refrigeration Repair", "provider": { "@id": canonical + "#org" }, "areaServed": [
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Los Angeles County" },
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Orange County" },
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Ventura County" },
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Santa Barbara County" }, { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "San Bernardino County" },
      { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "Riverside County" }, { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "San Diego County" }
    ], "description": "True Residential outdoor refrigeration repair across Los Angeles and the coast. UL-rated outdoor refrigerators, refrigerator and freezer drawers, beverage centers, 15-inch ice makers, and wine cabinets — condenser, forced-air cooling, fans, defrost, controls, and sealed-system service. Commercial-grade American-made refrigeration for the patio and BBQ island. $89 diagnostic, waived with repair." },
  { "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": faqs.map(f => ({ "@type": "Question", "name": f.q, "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": f.a.replace(/<[^>]+>/g, '') } })) },
  { "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [ { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://samedayappliance.repair/" }, { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Brands", "item": "https://samedayappliance.repair/brands/" }, { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "True Outdoor Refrigerator Repair", "item": canonical } ] }
] };

const wave46OrgSchema = mergeCredentials({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'HomeAndConstructionBusiness',
  '@id': canonical + '#org',
  name: 'Same Day Appliance Repair',
  url: canonical,
  priceRange: '$$',
  openingHoursSpecification: OPENING_HOURS_SCHEMA,
  areaServed: [
    { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Los Angeles County' },
    { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Orange County' },
    { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Ventura County' },
    { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Santa Barbara County' }, { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'San Bernardino County' },
    { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Riverside County' }, { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'San Diego County' }
  ],
  location: BRANCH_LOCATIONS_GEO_NEUTRAL
});
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical}>
  <Fragment slot="head-scripts">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(wave46OrgSchema)} />
  </Fragment>

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />
  <div class="call-banner"><div class="wrap"><span>True outdoor fridge down? Same-day across LA:</span><a href={`tel:${MAIN_PHONE_TEL}`} class="phone-lg">{MAIN_PHONE}</a></div></div>
  <ServiceHero
    section="brands"
    slug="true-residential-outdoor-refrigerator-repair"
    eyebrow={"True Outdoor Refrigeration Repair"}
    title={"True Outdoor Refrigerator Repair, Los Angeles"}
    subtitle={description}
    heroImageTitle={"True Residential Outdoor Refrigeration Repair"}
  />

  <BrandBranchesGrid />
  <section class="trust-bar"><div class="wrap"><span>Licensed BHGS #A49573 · Insured</span><span>Same-day · 7 Southern California counties</span><span>$89 diagnostic · waived with repair</span></div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2>True outdoor refrigeration — commercial-grade, built for the patio</h2>
    <p>True is the independent, American-made refrigeration maker that's built commercial cooling since 1945, and True Residential brings that same engineering home. Its outdoor line is exactly what a real LA outdoor kitchen needs: every True undercounter unit is UL-rated for outdoor use, built commercial-grade in 300-series stainless with forced-air cooling that holds temperature through the temperature swings, humidity, and direct afternoon sun that would overwhelm an indoor-rated fridge left on the patio. When a True outdoor refrigerator, beverage center, or ice maker in a Malibu cabana or a Newport Beach BBQ island stops holding temperature, our techs diagnose it on those same commercial-refrigeration principles. $89 diagnostic, waived with repair, BHGS #A49573, EPA 608 Universal certified (#1346255700410).</p>
    <p>One clarification up front, because the True name spans two worlds: this page is True Residential's outdoor line — the home patio and BBQ-island units, residential scope. If you run a restaurant or bar with a True commercial unit, that's our commercial True refrigeration service instead. For a home outdoor True, you're in the right place, and the diagnosis is the same forced-air, heavy-duty refrigeration work True is known for.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap">
    <h2>True outdoor units we service</h2>
    <div class="model-grid">
      <div class="model-card"><h3>Outdoor refrigerators (24")</h3><p>Glass-door and solid-door UL-rated outdoor refrigerators. Condenser and coils, forced-air cooling, evaporator fan, defrost, controls, sealed system.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>Refrigerator &amp; freezer drawers</h3><p>Outdoor undercounter refrigerator and freezer drawers for the BBQ island. Cooling system, drawer seals, controls.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>Outdoor beverage centers</h3><p>UL-rated beverage refrigeration for the patio bar. Same forced-air cooling and control diagnosis.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>15" outdoor ice makers</h3><p>Outdoor undercounter ice makers — the refrigeration side plus the water-path and ice-harvest diagnosis (inlet, fill, harvest, bin).</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>Outdoor wine cabinets</h3><p>Temperature-controlled outdoor wine refrigeration — cooling system, sensors, and controls to hold the set temperature outdoors.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>Coil, forced-air &amp; sealed-system service</h3><p>The core diagnosis across all True outdoor units — dirty condenser coils (they clog faster outdoors), the forced-air system, fans, defrost, and the sealed system on the serious end.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2>Why True outdoor units fail — and what we check</h2>
    <p>Outdoor refrigeration works harder than indoor, so the failure pattern skews toward the cooling system and the environment. Our techs start where the outdoor conditions bite hardest: the condenser coils, which clog faster outdoors because the unit pulls in dust, pollen, and debris, and which our LA summers punish. Clogged coils are the most common reason a True outdoor unit slowly loses cooling, and clearing them is often the fix. From there it's the forced-air cooling system and fans, the defrost components, the controls, and on the serious end the sealed system or compressor.</p>
    <p>We also check the installation, because heat load matters outdoors: a unit crammed into a BBQ island without airflow, or sitting in full afternoon sun, works harder and fails sooner. Getting the ventilation right is part of a lasting repair. Because True is an active American manufacturer with real parts support and a strong LA service footprint, the parts for these repairs are obtainable, and a True outdoor unit is nearly always worth fixing rather than replacing.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2>Related True &amp; outdoor refrigeration pages</h2>
    <ul class="related-links">
      <li><a href="/brands/true-residential/">True Residential brand hub</a> — the full residential line, sizes, and why it is not the commercial True</li>
      <li><a href="/brands/true-residential-refrigerator-repair/">True Residential refrigerator repair Los Angeles</a> — the indoor home line</li>
      <li><a href="/brands/true-residential-wine-cooler-repair/">True Residential wine cooler repair Los Angeles</a></li>
      <li><a href="/brands/perlick-outdoor-refrigerator-repair/">Perlick outdoor refrigerator repair</a> · <a href="/brands/u-line-outdoor-refrigerator-repair/">U-Line outdoor refrigerator repair</a></li>
      <li><a href="/brands/sub-zero-outdoor-refrigerator-repair/">Sub-Zero outdoor refrigerator repair</a> · <a href="/brands/viking-outdoor-refrigerator-repair/">Viking outdoor refrigerator repair</a></li>
      <li><a href="/services/outdoor-refrigerator-repair/">All outdoor refrigerator repair in Los Angeles →</a></li>
      <li><a href="/malibu/">Malibu service area</a> · <a href="/newport-beach/">Newport Beach service area</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="wrap narrow"><h2>True outdoor refrigeration repair, frequently asked</h2>{faqs.map(f => <details class="faq"><summary>{f.q}</summary><p set:html={f.a}></p></details>)}</div></section>

  <section id="book" class="cta-bottom"><div class="wrap"><h2>True outdoor unit down? Call the branch nearest your home.</h2><p>Same-day across LA, the coast, Orange County, Ventura, San Bernardino, and Riverside. $89 diagnostic, waived with repair.</p></div></section>
</Layout>

<style>
  body { color: var(--text); } .wrap { max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; } .wrap.narrow { max-width: 820px; }
  h1 { font-size: 2.4rem; line-height: 1.15; margin: 12px 0 20px; color: var(--black); } h2 { font-size: 1.8rem; margin: 0 0 16px; color: var(--black); } h3 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin: 0 0 10px; color: var(--black); } p { line-height: 1.65; margin: 0 0 14px; }
  .call-banner { background: var(--red); color: #fff; padding: 10px 0; } .call-banner .wrap { display:flex; gap: 14px; align-items: center; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; } .call-banner .phone-lg { color:#fff; font-weight: 800; text-decoration: underline; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .trust-bar { background: var(--red); color: #fff; padding: 14px 0; } .trust-bar .wrap { display: flex; gap: 28px; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .section { padding: 56px 0; } .section.alt { background: var(--gray); }
  .model-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 24px; } .model-card { background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 20px; border-radius: 6px; }
  .related-links { list-style: none; padding: 0; } .related-links li { padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); } .related-links a { color: var(--red); font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; } .related-links a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .faq { background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 8px; border-radius: 4px; } .faq summary { font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer; padding: 4px 0; } .faq p { margin: 8px 0 0; }
  .cta-bottom { background: var(--black); color: #fff; padding: 48px 0; } .cta-bottom h2 { color: #fff; } .cta-bottom p { color: #c9c9c9; }
  @media (max-width: 820px) { h1 { font-size: 1.9rem; } h2 { font-size: 1.45rem; }  .trust-bar .wrap { gap: 14px; font-size: 0.85rem; } }
</style>
